"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Enterprise and Enterprise Advanced plans"
" <https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:6
msgid "plans-img-yellow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Experimental certificate-based authentication has been deprecated from "
"Mattermost v11.0.** From Mattermost v11, you must :ref:`disable this "
"feature <administration-guide/configure/experimental-configuration-"
"settings:enable client-side certification>` to start the server. Enabling"
" this setting will prevent the server from starting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:10
msgid ""
"Prior to v11, certificate-based authentication (CBA) is available as an "
"experimental feature to identify a user or a device before granting "
"access to Mattermost and provide an additional layer of security to "
"access the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:12
msgid ""
"Before you begin, follow the :doc:`official guides to install Mattermost "
"</deployment-guide/deployment-guide-index>` on your system, including "
"NGINX configuration as a proxy with SSL and HTTP/2, and a valid SSL "
"certificate such as Let's Encrypt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:14
msgid ""
"Then, follow the steps below to configure user CBA for your browser and "
"Mattermost Desktop Apps. You can manage certificate distribution for each"
" personal device (BYOD) and their life cycle management with a service "
"like `OpenSSL <https://www.openssl.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:17
msgid "Set up mutual TLS authentication for the Web App"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:19
msgid ""
":doc:`Setting up mutual TLS authentication </administration-guide/onboard"
"/ssl-client-certificate>` is the first step to set up certificate-based "
"authentication."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:22
msgid "Set up Mattermost server to log in with a client certificate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:24
msgid ""
"Make sure your Mattermost server is licensed with a valid Enterprise "
"license."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:25
msgid ""
"In ``ExperimentalSettings`` of the ``config.json`` file, set "
"``ClientSideCertEnable`` to ``true`` and ``ClientSideCertCheck`` to one "
"of the following values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:27
msgid ""
"``primary`` - After the client side certificate is verified, user's email"
" is retrieved from the certificate and is used to log in without a "
"password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:28
msgid ""
"``secondary`` - After the client side certificate is verified, user's "
"email is retrieved from the certificate and matched against the one "
"supplied by the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:30
msgid "If they match, the user logs in with regular email/password credentials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:32
msgid "The ``config.json`` file should then have the following lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:41
msgid "Restart the Mattermost server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/administration-guide/onboard/certificate-based-authentication.rst:43
msgid ""
"Go to ``https://example.mattermost.com`` and try to log in. The server "
"should require the x.509 cert to have an ``emailAddress`` equal to the "
"Mattermost user's email."
msgstr ""

